{"id":"173103b981643051","group":"93","path":"93/93-thm-algebraizable-criterion.md","title":"Algebraizability Criterion","display":"Algebraizability Criterion","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-thm-algebraizable-criterion","aliases":["93-thm-algebraizable-criterion"],"display":"Algebraizability Criterion","depends_on":["[[93-df-algebraizable]]","[[93-df-logic]]","[[93-df-equivalent]]","[[93-df-equivalence-formula]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-thm-algebraizable-criterion"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-thm-algebraizable-criterion</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"Algebraizability Criterion"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a55351eb48f8bd69\" href=\"?note=a55351eb48f8bd69\" title=\"93-df-algebraizable\">93-df-algebraizable</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"7cb391918869c9ba\" href=\"?note=7cb391918869c9ba\" title=\"93-df-equivalent\">93-df-equivalent</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"f1eab1108defb738\" href=\"?note=f1eab1108defb738\" title=\"93-df-equivalence-formula\">93-df-equivalence-formula</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"thm-algebraizable-criterion-—-Algebraizability-Criterion\">thm-algebraizable-criterion — Algebraizability Criterion</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L\">\\(\\mathcal L\\)</span> is a propositional-logic candidate.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AlgLog}\">\\(\\mathrm{AlgLog}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}\\)</span> are the class and two-translation predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"a55351eb48f8bd69\" href=\"?note=a55351eb48f8bd69\" title=\"93-df-algebraizable\">93-df-algebraizable</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}algebraizable\\text{-}criterion}\\vdash\n\\mathcal L\\in\\mathrm{AlgLog}\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\exists\\mathbf K\\;\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathbf K;\\tau)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}algebraizable\\text{-}criterion}\\vdash\n\\mathcal L\\in\\mathrm{AlgLog}\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\exists\\mathbf K\\;\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathbf K;\\tau)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Here <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}\\)</span> already requires a quasivariety and the two finite translations. Requiring the equivalent algebraic semantics to be a variety would incorrectly exclude algebraizable logics whose canonical semantics is only quasivarietal.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"thm-algebraizable-criterion-—-Algebraizability-Criterion","text":"thm-algebraizable-criterion — Algebraizability Criterion","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-algebraizable","status":"resolved","id":"a55351eb48f8bd69","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-algebraizable]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-logic","status":"resolved","id":"bd7e4207897c8db3","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-logic]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-equivalent","status":"resolved","id":"7cb391918869c9ba","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-equivalent]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-equivalence-formula","status":"resolved","id":"f1eab1108defb738","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-equivalence-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebraizable","status":"resolved","id":"a55351eb48f8bd69","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{AlgLog}$ and $\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}$ are the class and two-translation predicate of [[93-df-algebraizable]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{AlgLog}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}algebraizable\\text{-}criterion}\\vdash\n\\mathcal L\\in\\mathrm{AlgLog}\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\tau\\;\\exists\\mathbf K\\;\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}(\\mathcal L,\\mathbf K;\\tau)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Algz}_{93}","display":false}],"bytes":1020,"backlinks":[],"outgoing":["a55351eb48f8bd69","bd7e4207897c8db3","7cb391918869c9ba","f1eab1108defb738"]}